      "description": "Careers Skip to Main Content Press Control+M to start dragging object ptnbsid=T6YcQHZyAHGyARFA2RIbt9xjtFU%3d Back Abraham Baldwin Agricultural College Careers Search Category Name Search keywords Search in... Menu Category All Company Directory Job Data No results to display Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Actions Search My Preferences Help Sign Out Abraham Baldwin Agricultural College Careers More Actions Welcome Sign In New User Thank you for your interest in opportunities at Abraham Baldwin Agricultural College. You can search and review all opportunities from this page without creating an account with us. When you are ready to apply, login or create a new applicant account. You can access this applicant portal on your desktop, laptop, or any mobile device, and you will be able to: View all job opportunities Search on specific criteria to find jobs that interest you Set up a search agent that will notify you when positions are posted that match your search criteria. For technical support or assistance completing a job application, please contact the USG Service Desk at (877) 251-2644 or support@usg.edu . For questions about opportunities at Abraham Baldwin Agricultural College, please contact Human Resources at 229-391-4887  and/or HR@abac.edu . Due to an Oracle Known Issue, Mac OS users are advised to browse and apply for jobs using a web browser other than Safari. The Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act and the Higher Education Act (HEA) fire safety provisions require institutions of higher education to publish an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report. These reports include crime and fire statistics for the three most recently completed calendar years, institutional policies and procedures for reporting crimes, and current policies concerning the security of, and access to, campus facilities and residences, as well as security considerations in the maintenance of campus facilities. The reports are available online at: https://www.abac.edu/_documents/police-department/abac-2025-annual-security-report-updated-9-25.pdf . If you would like to retain a copy of the report, you may print it from your browser or request a paper copy by emailing the institution at mtompkins@abac.edu . View All Jobs My Job Notifications My Job Applications My Favorite Jobs My Saved Searches My Account Information Abraham Baldwin Agricultural College Careers Sign In New User"
